From 5bce48ed9281cb496efa5c5f766b0787a9974fd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZonicExists <71136987+zonicisalive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:28:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 39/42] bitproxy: log in to VPN providers

One card for providers with an API to get WireGuard servers: Mullvad
(account number), IVPN (account ID, optional 2FA), Private Internet
Access (username/password, addKey with PIA's own CA), AirVPN (API key,
generated configs), AzireVPN (v3 token + IP), NordVPN (access token,
NordLynx key) and Cloudflare WARP (anonymous registration).

Each login writes plain .conf files into BitProxyStore, so the servers
work like imported ones. Log out removes the key or device on the
provider where it has one.
